creating notebooks for data exploration  for creating educational content  or even writing full-on research papers  is always fun  but to make sure that the content is  reproducible across all systems  is kind of tricky with nvidia videos  we're trying to solve  some of these issues the main motivation  behind mpg produce is to make sure  that domain experts who are not  necessarily devops or programming  experts  are able to create usable content from  their research projects  even with tools like condi and pep  available locally  to make sure that the local environment  is  set up correctly across different  systems is hard the current use case of  uh mbt produce is to make sure that we  have a one click or one command  reproduction of a research paper or a  replication of a research paper  in a containerized environment the  figures that we get  today from running a script or a  notebook should be the same  figures that we get 10 years on the line  and with nb reviews  we try to achieve that the main features  of mb reviews  is that it lets you reproduce a notebook  inside a container  which is created using a docker image it  also lets you  start up a jupyter lab instance inside a  docker container  which again builds upon our docker image  and it also lets you  reproduce entire projects using a bash  file or  some sort of a make file uh it doesn't  just needs to be a notebook it could be  it could be  a c file it could be some julia code it  could be latex files  could be the paper itself that needs to  be compiled  and nvidia use is available on wi-fi  and you can install it using pip install  npd produce  it does require docker to be installed  locally so if you're on  windows or mac there is stopper desktop  available for you  and if you are on linux you have docker  engine available for you  and let's have a quick demo of nbd  produce  so nd reproduce can fetch  uh urls it can fetch uh it can run local  uh notebooks so in this case we fetch a  url from github  which is just a hello world example of a  notebook  and when we do when we run this command  it will download the jupyter notebook  from the  from the url it will try to execute the  notebook  inside inside a container using this  environment and if you  if you look at this thing it says  jupiter sci-fi notebook latest  it's one of the standard uh docker  images from the jupiter topper stacks  and nvidia produce knows to look for  this image because nba reproduce  uh inserts uh and inserts a docker image  tab  inside every notebook in the metadata if  you look at the raw format of this  hello world dot  [Music]  which is ipv here if you if you look at  the metadata you could see this  tag docker image and it points towards  this  uh docker image which is hosted on  docker hub  and we can see that it has executed the  notebook and  by default nvidia videos will create a  copy of the image and it will  uh append reproduce at the end of  the end of the name of the notebook and  we can also open up the notebook to see  how it looks like  reproduced one when we click on it it  will  [Music]  yep this is how it looks like so we have  the images are the images are reproduced  and we can see them here  the other feature of nvgpus is that you  can start up  uh you can start up a jupiter lab or  jupiter  notebook instance by default if we do  npd produce live it will start with  jupiter lab instance  and just just like how you start a  jupiter lab on  in the command line  [Music]  let's wait for url  so nvidia videos live will start a  jupiter lab instance inside the docker  container  so you have the environment available  from the docker  container rather than your laptop or  your desktop  watch url here right here let's click on  this  and this will open up a jupyter lab  instance  and let's go into work by default it  means the directory as work  and this can be changed but  as we click on the notebook we can see  we have  a reproduced notebook available we also  have